    /// step → the screen's words, in order, single-spaced
    static let sections: [String: String] = [
        "welcome": "Your Hermes, wherever you are. Chat with your agents, see what they’re working on, and get a ping when they’re done, right from your iPhone. Hermes stays on your computer. Your agents, chats and files stay there. Hermes HQ connects your iPhone to it. Set it up once; it takes a few minutes. Only you can get in. Hermes HQ never stores your password. Get Started I already have an address",
        "where": "Back Set it up yourself Where does Hermes run? Pick the computer Hermes is installed on. On a MacOne command sets it up. Then you sign in with your Nous account. On Linux or a serverThe same one command, run there or over SSH. Then you sign in with Nous. On WindowsUses Tailscale, a free app, on that computer and this iPhone, with a password. Someone gave me an addressSign in with the address and details they sent you. No Hermes yet? It runs on a computer, not on your phone. Install Hermes first, then come back.",
        "hermes": "Let Hermes set it up. Send this message to your Hermes, wherever you chat with it: Telegram, Discord, the Hermes app or its terminal. Hermes sets up its own computer for you. Copy Message Send… Show the message Please connect this computer to Hermes HQ, the iPhone app for Hermes, so I can reach you from anywhere and sign in with my Nous account. Run this in your terminal, on this computer itself (if your terminal runs in a container, sandbox or another machine, stop and tell me): curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrcharlesiv/hermes-hq/main/connect.sh | sh -s -- --agent It's safe to run again and again. Each time it either finishes or prints a NEXT STEP. If the next step is for you, do it. If it's for me (a link to open, a code, or a command that needs my password), send it to me word for word and wait until I say I've done it. Then run the command again, until it says DONE. It uses Tailscale on this computer (free) to give it an address my phone can reach; my phone doesn't need Tailscale. Never send me files from this computer, and put any file path you mention in backticks. When it says DONE, send me the address it prints and tell me to paste it into Hermes HQ and tap Sign in with Nous. If it says it can't run on this computer, tell me why. Hermes runs the setup on its computer. It may send you a link or two to sign in to, both free: Nous, so only you can get in, and Tailscale, which gives that computer an address your iPhone can reach from anywhere. When it’s done, Hermes sends you the address. Paste it on the next screen and tap Sign in with Nous. Tailscale runs only on that computer: nothing to install on this iPhone. Works when Hermes runs on a Mac or Linux, servers included. I Have the Address Set It Up Myself",
        "mac-1": "Step 1 of 3 Get the setup command onto your Mac. You’ll paste one line into Terminal on your Mac. It sets up everything else for you. curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrcharlesiv/hermes-hq/main/connect.sh | sh Copy Send to Your Mac… Or on your Mac, open github.com/mrcharlesiv/hermes-hq in a web browser and copy the command from there. Next",
        "mac-2": "Step 2 of 3 Run it in Terminal on your Mac. Open Terminal: press ⌘ Space, type Terminal, then press Return. Paste the command with ⌘ V, then press Return. Do what it asks. It signs this Mac in to Nous, so only you can get in, and to Tailscale, which gives your Mac an address this iPhone can reach from anywhere (both free). It may open your browser for you to sign in, or ask you to click Allow. It takes about five minutes. Tailscale runs only on your Mac: your iPhone doesn’t need it. If you stop partway, run the command again: it picks up where it left off. If Terminal shows a problem “Hermes isn’t installed” Install Hermes on this Mac first (Hermes setup guide), then run the command again. “Hermes didn’t start in the background” Open a new Terminal window with ⌘ N, type hermes serve and press Return. Leave it running, then run the command again in the first one. “Needs Node.js 20 or newer” Update Hermes: type hermes update and press Return, then run the command again. “Turn on MagicDNS and HTTPS Certificates” Open the link it shows, switch both on, then run the command again. “Restart Hermes now” Stop Hermes where you started it (Control C in its window) and start it again the same way. The setup carries on by itself. Anything else Run the command again; that’s always safe. Still stuck? Paste what the terminal says into a chat with Hermes and ask it for help. Next",
        "mac-3": "Step 3 of 3 Scan the QR code with this iPhone. When the setup is done, Terminal shows a QR code. It holds your Mac’s address, so you don’t have to type it. Open the Camera app and point it at the QR code on the screen. Tap Open in Hermes HQ. Tap Sign in with Nous, with the same Nous account you used on your Mac. Keep your Mac on and awake: Hermes HQ can reach Hermes only while it is. Type the Address Instead",
        "linux-1": "Step 1 of 3 Get the setup command onto that computer. You’ll paste one line into a terminal on the computer running Hermes, or into an SSH session to it. It sets up everything else for you. curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mrcharlesiv/hermes-hq/main/connect.sh | sh Copy Send… Or on the computer you’ll type it on, open github.com/mrcharlesiv/hermes-hq in a web browser and copy the command from there. Next",
        "linux-2": "Step 2 of 3 Run it in a terminal there. Open a terminal on the computer running Hermes, or connect to it with SSH. Paste the command and press Enter. Do what it asks. It signs that computer in to Nous, so only you can get in, and to Tailscale, which gives it an address this iPhone can reach from anywhere (both free). It may show a link to open in any browser (this iPhone’s is fine), or ask for your password once. It takes about five minutes. Tailscale runs only on that computer: your iPhone doesn’t need it. If you stop partway, run the command again: it picks up where it left off. If the terminal shows a problem “Hermes isn’t installed” Install Hermes on that computer first (Hermes setup guide), then run the command again. “Hermes didn’t start in the background” In a second terminal, type hermes serve and press Enter. Leave it running, then run the command again in the first one. “Tailscale is installed but not signed in” Type sudo tailscale up, open the link it shows and sign in, then run the command again. “systemd user services … can’t reach” Log in to that computer directly or over SSH as yourself, not with su or sudo, then run the command again. “Turn on MagicDNS and HTTPS Certificates” Open the link it shows, switch both on, then run the command again. “Restart Hermes now” Stop Hermes where you started it (Control C in its window) and start it again the same way. The setup carries on by itself. Anything else Run the command again; that’s always safe. Still stuck? Paste what the terminal says into a chat with Hermes and ask it for help. Next",
        "linux-3": "Step 3 of 3 Scan the QR code with this iPhone. When the setup is done, the terminal shows a QR code. It holds that computer’s address, so you don’t have to type it. Open the Camera app and point it at the QR code on the screen. Tap Open in Hermes HQ. Tap Sign in with Nous, with the same Nous account you used there. Keep that computer on: Hermes HQ can reach Hermes only while it is. Type the Address Instead",
        "other-1": "Step 1 of 2 Install Tailscale on both. Tailscale is a free app that privately links this iPhone and the computer running Hermes, wherever you are. On this iPhone: install Tailscale and sign in.Get Tailscale On the computer running Hermes: install Tailscale from tailscale.com/download and sign in with the same account. Next",
        "other-2": "Step 2 of 2 Let Hermes do the setup. Copy this message and send it to Hermes on that computer, wherever you chat with it: in its terminal, Telegram, Discord or the Hermes app. Copy Message for Hermes Show the message Please set up this computer so I can use Hermes from Hermes HQ, the iPhone app for Hermes. Use your terminal tools and do each step yourself; stop and ask me only for what you can't do. If your terminal runs somewhere other than this computer (a container, sandbox or remote machine), stop and tell me. 1. Check that Tailscale is installed, running and signed in (tailscale status). If it isn't, tell me how to install it and sign in, and wait for me. Remind me to install Tailscale on my phone with the same account, and to turn on MagicDNS and HTTPS certificates in the Tailscale admin console (https://login.tailscale.com/admin/dns). 2. Run tailscale serve status. If nothing is being served, run: tailscale serve --bg 9119 If something is already served, don't replace it; run tailscale serve --bg --https=8443 9119 instead and use :8443 in the address. The address is https:// plus this computer's MagicDNS name (Self.DNSName in tailscale status --json, without the trailing dot), e.g. https://your-computer.your-tailnet.ts.net 3. Ask me for the username and password I want to type into Hermes HQ, or offer to generate a strong password. These are sign-in details for this computer's Hermes, not an AI provider login. Generate a secret with: openssl rand -base64 32 4. Back up ~/.hermes/.env, then set these four lines in it (replace any existing values for the same keys, don't duplicate them): HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME=your-username HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD=your-long-password HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_SECRET=the-secret-you-generated HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-computer.your-tailnet.ts.net using my username and password, the secret from step 3 and the address from step 2 (with :8443 if you used it). 5. Start the dashboard so it keeps running after this chat ends: hermes dashboard --no-open (in the background, e.g. with nohup, or as a login service). If a dashboard is already running, restart it so it reads the new settings. 6. Check it: curl -sI on the address should answer, not \"400 Invalid Host header\". If it fails, fix it and check again. When you're done, tell me in plain words the address and username to type into Hermes HQ, and anything I still have to do myself. Don't repeat the password back in the chat. Hermes does the setup, has you choose a password, then tells you the address and username to sign in with. I’d rather do it myself Next: Sign In",
        "manual": "Without Hermes’s help Set it up yourself. Type these on the computer running Hermes, not on this iPhone. Tailscale should already be on both, signed in to the same account, with MagicDNS and HTTPS Certificates turned on in its admin console. Copy All Steps Share Hermes on your Tailscale network tailscale serve --bg 9119 It prints your address, like https://your-computer.your-tailnet.ts.net. If this computer already shares something with Tailscale Serve, this replaces it: use --https=8443 instead and add :8443 to the address. Tailscale Serve guide Turn on sign-in Make a secret: openssl rand -base64 32 Add four lines to the file ~/.hermes/.env, with your own username, password, that secret and the address from step 1: HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME=your-username HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD=your-long-password HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_SECRET=the-secret-you-generated HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-computer.your-tailnet.ts.net You choose this username and password here; they aren’t your AI provider’s login. Without the last line, Hermes turns your phone away. Sign-in guide Start Hermes Run this and leave it running. Restart it whenever you change those lines. hermes dashboard --no-open Next: Sign In",
    ]
}
